To create an Elastic Beanstalk Worker Environment for running batch processing jobs, we need to set up several AWS resources including an IAM role and instance profile, an S3 bucket, an SQS queue, and the Elastic Beanstalk application and environment. Below is the Terraform HCL configuration that accomplishes this:

### Description:
- **IAM Role (`eb_ec2_role`)**: This role will be attached to the EC2 instances in the Elastic Beanstalk Worker Environment. It will have policies to allow access to S3 and SQS.
- **Instance Profile (`eb_ec2_profile`)**: This profile will be associated with the IAM role.
- **Elastic Beanstalk Application (`batch_job_app`)**: This is the main application that will contain the worker environment.
- **S3 Bucket (`sampleapril26426`)**: A storage bucket where the batch job files can be stored.
- **S3 Object (`examplebucket_object`)**: An example object inside the S3 bucket.
- **SQS Queue (`batch_job_queue`)**: A queue that will be used by the worker environment to receive messages and process them.
- **Elastic Beanstalk Application Version (`version`)**: The version of the application that will be deployed.

### Terraform Configuration:

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

# IAM Role for EC2 instances in Elastic Beanstalk Worker Environment
resource "aws_iam_role" "eb_ec2_role" {
  name = "eb_ec2_role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "ec2.amazonaws.com"
        }
      },
    ]
  })
}

# Attach necessary policies to the IAM role
resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "s3_access" {
  policy_arn = "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AmazonS3ReadOnlyAccess"
  role       = aws_iam_role.eb_ec2_role.name
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "sqs_access" {
  policy_arn = "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/service-role/AWSElasticBeanstalkWorkerSQSServiceRolePolicy"
  role       = aws_iam_role.eb_ec2_role.name
}

# Instance Profile for the IAM role
resource "aws_iam_instance_profile" "eb_ec2_profile" {
  name = "eb_ec2_profile"
  role = aws_iam_role.eb_ec2_role.name
}

# Elastic Beanstalk Application
resource "aws_elastic_beanstalk_application" "batch_job_app" {
  name        = "batch_job_app"
  description = "Application for running batch processing jobs"
}

# S3 Bucket
resource "aws_s3_bucket" "sampleapril26426" {
  bucket = "sampleapril26426"
}

# S3 Object
resource "aws_s3_bucket_object" "examplebucket_object" {
  bucket = aws_s3_bucket.sampleapril26426.id
  key    = "example_object.txt"
  source = "path/to/local/file.txt"
}

# SQS Queue
resource "aws_sqs_queue" "batch_job_queue" {
  name = "batch_job_queue"
}

# Elastic Beanstalk Application Version
resource "aws_elastic_beanstalk_application_version" "version" {
  application = aws_elastic_beanstalk_application.batch_job_app.name
  name        = "version"
  bucket      = aws_s3_bucket.sampleapril26426.id
  key         = aws_s3_bucket_object.examplebucket_object.key
}

# Elastic Beanstalk Worker Environment
resource "aws_elastic_beanstalk_environment" "worker_env" {
  name                = "worker-env"
  application         = aws_elastic_beanstalk_application.batch_job_app.name
  solution_stack_name = "64bit Amazon Linux 2 v5.7.0 running Java 8"
  version_label       = aws_elastic_beanstalk_application_version.version.name

  setting {
    namespace = "aws:autoscaling:asg"
    option_name = "MinSize"
    value       = "1"
  }

  setting {
    namespace = "aws:autoscaling:asg"
    option_name = "MaxSize"
    value       = "4"
  }

  setting {
    namespace = "aws:elasticbeanstalk:sqsd"
    option_name = "QueueName"
    value       = aws_sqs_queue.batch_job_queue.name
  }

  setting {
    namespace = "aws:elasticbeanstalk:environment"
    option_name = "EnvironmentType"
    value       = "SingleInstance"
  }

  setting {
    namespace = "aws:autoscaling:launchconfiguration"
    option_name = "IamInstanceProfile"
    value       = aws_iam_instance_profile.eb_ec2_profile.name
  }
}
```

### Notes:
- Ensure that the `source` attribute in the `aws_s3_bucket_object` resource points to a valid local file path.
- The `solution_stack_name` can be adjusted based on the specific runtime and platform requirements of your batch processing jobs.
- The `EnvironmentType` is set to `SingleInstance` for simplicity; you may want to adjust this for production environments.
- The `MinSize` and `MaxSize` settings control the auto-scaling behavior of the environment. Adjust these values as needed for your use case.

