### Description

The Terraform program will create an AWS Elastic Beanstalk application along with an application version lifecycle configuration. The application version lifecycle configuration will specify how many versions of the application to retain and whether to delete source bundles when the application versions are deleted.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

# Define the Elastic Beanstalk application
resource "aws_elastic_beanstalk_application" "example_app" {
  name        = "example-application"
  description = "An example Elastic Beanstalk application"
}

# Define the application version lifecycle configuration
resource "aws_elastic_beanstalk_application_version_lifecycle" "example_app_lifecycle" {
  application = aws_elastic_beanstalk_application.example_app.name

  max_count = 5
  delete_source_from_s3 = true

  # Optional: Define a service role for managing the lifecycle
  service_role = aws_iam_role.example_app_lifecycle_role.arn
}

# Create an IAM role for the application version lifecycle management
resource "aws_iam_role" "example_app_lifecycle_role" {
  name = "example-app-lifecycle-role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "elasticbeanstalk.amazonaws.com"
        }
      },
    ]
  })
}

# Attach necessary policies to the IAM role
resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "example_app_lifecycle_policy" {
  policy_arn = "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/service-role/AWSElasticBeanstalkEnhancedHealth"
  role       = aws_iam_role.example_app_lifecycle_role.name
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "example_app_lifecycle_policy_s3" {
  policy_arn = "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AmazonS3FullAccess"
  role       = aws_iam_role.example_app_lifecycle_role.name
}
```

### Explanation

1. **Provider Configuration**: Specifies the AWS region (`us-west-2` in this case).
2. **Elastic Beanstalk Application**: Creates an Elastic Beanstalk application named `example-application`.
3. **Application Version Lifecycle Configuration**: Configures the lifecycle of application versions for the Elastic Beanstalk application. It retains up to 5 versions and deletes the source bundle from S3 when the application versions are deleted.
4. **IAM Role for Lifecycle Management**: Creates an IAM role that allows Elastic Beanstalk to manage the application version lifecycle.
5. **IAM Role Policy Attachments**: Attaches policies to the IAM role to allow it to perform necessary actions, such as accessing S3 and managing enhanced health features in Elastic Beanstalk.

This configuration ensures that the Elastic Beanstalk application is set up with a managed lifecycle for its application versions, including automatic cleanup of old versions and their associated S3 source bundles.

