Certainly! Below is a Terraform configuration that creates an AWS CodeBuild project with an associated IAM role and a Batch configuration. The IAM role will have the necessary permissions for CodeBuild to interact with other AWS services, and the Batch configuration will allow the use of AWS Batch for running batch builds.

### Description:
- **Provider Configuration**: Configured for AWS with a specific region.
- **IAM Role**: Created specifically for the CodeBuild project with policies attached to allow it to interact with S3, EC2, and AWS Batch.
- **CodeBuild Project**: Configured to use the created IAM role and includes a Batch configuration to run builds using AWS Batch.

### Terraform HCL Configuration:

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"  # You can change this to your preferred region
}

# Create an IAM role for CodeBuild
resource "aws_iam_role" "codebuild_role" {
  name = "codebuild-role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "codebuild.amazonaws.com"
        }
      },
    ]
  })
}

# Attach necessary policies to the IAM role
resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "codebuild_policy_s3" {
  policy_arn = "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AmazonS3ReadOnlyAccess"
  role       = aws_iam_role.codebuild_role.name
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "codebuild_policy_ec2" {
  policy_arn = "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/service-role/AWSCodeBuildEC2ContainerServiceforAWSCodePipeline"
  role       = aws_iam_role.codebuild_role.name
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "codebuild_policy_batch" {
  policy_arn = "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AWSBatchFullAccess"
  role       = aws_iam_role.codebuild_role.name
}

# Create a CodeBuild project
resource "aws_codebuild_project" "example" {
  name          = "example-codebuild-project"
  description   = "An example CodeBuild project with Batch configuration"
  service_role  = aws_iam_role.codebuild_role.arn

  artifacts {
    type = "NO_ARTIFACTS"
  }

  environment {
    compute_type = "BUILD_GENERAL1_SMALL"
    image        = "aws/codebuild/standard:6.0"
    type         = "LINUX_CONTAINER"
    privileged_mode = true
  }

  source {
    type     = "GITHUB"
    location = "https://github.com/example/repo.git"
    git_clone_depth = 1
    auth {
      type = "OAUTH"
      resource = var.github_oauth_token
    }
  }

  vpc_config {
    subnets         = ["subnet-12345678", "subnet-87654321"]  # Replace with your subnet IDs
    security_groups = ["sg-12345678"]                         # Replace with your security group ID
    vpc_id          = "vpc-12345678"                          # Replace with your VPC ID
  }

  logs_config {
    cloudwatch_logs {
      status = "ENABLED"
      group_name = "/aws/codebuild/example-codebuild-project"
      stream_name = "build-log-stream"
    }
  }

  build_batch_config {
    combine_artifacts = false
    service_role      = aws_iam_role.codebuild_role.arn
    timeout_in_minutes = 60
  }
}

# Variable for GitHub OAuth token
variable "github_oauth_token" {
  description = "GitHub OAuth token for repository access"
  type        = string
  default     = ""  # It's recommended to set this value via environment variable or tfvars file
}
```

### Notes:
- **Region**: The region is set to `us-west-2`, but you can change it to any region that suits your needs.
- **IAM Policies**: The IAM role is attached with policies that provide read-only access to S3, full access to AWS Batch, and necessary permissions for CodeBuild to interact with EC2.
- **CodeBuild Source**: The source is configured to pull from a GitHub repository. You need to replace the `location` URL with your actual GitHub repository URL and provide a GitHub OAuth token via the `github_oauth_token` variable.
- **VPC Configuration**: The VPC configuration is set up with example subnet, security group, and VPC IDs. Replace these with your actual VPC details.
- **Build Batch Configuration**: The build batch configuration is enabled with a timeout of 60 minutes. Adjust this as needed.

This configuration is ready to be deployed with Terraform version `~> 1.9.8` and the AWS provider version `~> 5.75`.

