To create an AWS Lex V2 bot using Terraform, we need to define several resources including the IAM role that Lex will assume, the bot itself, and its associated intents and slots if necessary. For simplicity, I'll create a basic bot without intents and slots, focusing on setting up the bot and its IAM role.

### Description:
This Terraform configuration will create an AWS Lex V2 bot named "MyLexBot". It will also create an IAM role that the Lex bot can assume, granting it the necessary permissions to operate. The bot will be configured with a simple voice and text locale (en_US).

