To create a Kinesis Firehose Delivery Stream with an OpenSearch Serverless Destination using Terraform, we need to set up several AWS resources:

1. **IAM Role and Policy**: The Firehose delivery stream needs an IAM role with policies that allow it to write to OpenSearch Serverless and perform other necessary actions.
2. **Kinesis Firehose Delivery Stream**: This is the main resource that will deliver data to the OpenSearch Serverless destination.
3. **OpenSearch Serverless Collection**: This is where the data from the Firehose stream will be delivered.

Below is the Terraform HCL configuration that accomplishes this:

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"  # You can change this to your preferred region
}

# Create an OpenSearch Serverless Collection
resource "aws_opensearchserverless_collection" "example" {
  name        = "example-collection"
  description = "Example OpenSearch Serverless Collection for Kinesis Firehose"
}

# Create an IAM role for Kinesis Firehose
resource "aws_iam_role" "firehose_role" {
  name = "firehose-to-opensearch-role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "firehose.amazonaws.com"
        }
      },
    ]
  })
}

# Attach necessary policies to the IAM role
resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "firehose_policy" {
  policy_arn = "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AmazonKinesisFirehoseFullAccess"
  role       = aws_iam_role.firehose_role.name
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "opensearch_policy" {
  policy_arn = "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AmazonOpenSearchServerlessReadOnlyAccess"
  role       = aws_iam_role.firehose_role.name
}

# Create a Kinesis Firehose Delivery Stream with OpenSearch Serverless as the destination
resource "aws_kinesis_firehose_delivery_stream" "example" {
  name        = "example-firehose-stream"
  destination = "opensearchserverless"

  opensearchserverless_configuration {
    collection_endpoint = aws_opensearchserverless_collection.example.collection_endpoint
    index_name          = "example-index"
    role_arn            = aws_iam_role.firehose_role.arn

    buffering_hints {
      interval_in_seconds = 300
      size_in_megabytes   = 5
    }

    processing_configuration {
      enabled = false
    }

    s3_backup_mode = "Disabled"
  }
}
```

### Explanation:
- **Provider Configuration**: Specifies the AWS region.
- **OpenSearch Serverless Collection**: Creates a new OpenSearch Serverless collection.
- **IAM Role**: Creates an IAM role that Kinesis Firehose can assume.
- **IAM Role Policy Attachments**: Attaches policies to the IAM role to allow Firehose to write to OpenSearch Serverless and perform other necessary actions.
- **Kinesis Firehose Delivery Stream**: Configures the Firehose delivery stream to send data to the OpenSearch Serverless collection.

