LLM Output #0:
To create a Kinesis Firehose Delivery Stream with an HTTP endpoint destination (e.g., New Relic), we need to set up several AWS resources:

1. **IAM Role**: An IAM role with permissions to allow Kinesis Firehose to send data to the HTTP endpoint.
2. **Kinesis Firehose Delivery Stream**: The main resource that will deliver data to the specified HTTP endpoint.

Below is the Terraform HCL configuration that accomplishes this:

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"  # You can change this to your preferred region
}

# IAM Role for Kinesis Firehose to send data to HTTP endpoint
resource "aws_iam_role" "firehose_delivery_role" {
  name = "firehose-delivery-role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "firehose.amazonaws.com"
        }
      },
    ]
  })
}

# IAM Policy for Kinesis Firehose to send data to HTTP endpoint
resource "aws_iam_policy" "firehose_delivery_policy" {
  name        = "firehose-delivery-policy"
  description = "Policy for Kinesis Firehose to send data to HTTP endpoint"

  policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = [
          "logs:CreateLogGroup",
          "logs:CreateLogStream",
          "logs:PutLogEvents"
        ]
        Effect   = "Allow"
        Resource = "arn:aws:logs:*:*:*"
      },
      {
        Action = [
          "http:Post"
        ]
        Effect   = "Allow"
        Resource = "*"  # This should be restricted to the specific HTTP endpoint URL if possible
      }
    ]
  })
}

# Attach the policy to the IAM role
resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "firehose_delivery_policy_attachment" {
  policy_arn = aws_iam_policy.firehose_delivery_policy.arn
  role       = aws_iam_role.firehose_delivery_role.name
}

# Kinesis Firehose Delivery Stream with HTTP endpoint destination
resource "aws_kinesis_firehose_delivery_stream" "http_endpoint_delivery_stream" {
  name        = "http-endpoint-delivery-stream"
  destination = "http_endpoint"

  http_endpoint_configuration {
    url                = "https://your-http-endpoint-url.com"  # Replace with your HTTP endpoint URL
    name               = "http-endpoint-destination"
    role_arn           = aws_iam_role.firehose_delivery_role.arn
    buffering_hints {
      size_in_megabytes = 5
      interval_in_seconds = 300
    }
    request_configuration {
      content_encoding = "GZIP"
    }
  }

  # Optional: S3 backup configuration
  s3_configuration {
    bucket_arn = "arn:aws:s3:::your-s3-bucket-name"  # Replace with your S3 bucket ARN
    role_arn   = aws_iam_role.firehose_delivery_role.arn
  }
}
```

### Explanation:
- **Provider Configuration**: Specifies the AWS region where the resources will be created.
- **IAM Role**: Allows Kinesis Firehose to assume the role necessary to send data to the HTTP endpoint.
- **IAM Policy**: Grants the necessary permissions for logging and sending data to the HTTP endpoint.
- **IAM Role Policy Attachment**: Attaches the policy to the IAM role.
- **Kinesis Firehose Delivery Stream**: Configures the delivery stream to send data to the specified HTTP endpoint. It includes buffering hints and request configuration settings. An optional S3 backup configuration is also included, which you can modify or remove based on your requirements.

Make sure to replace `"https://your-http-endpoint-url.com"` and `"arn:aws:s3:::your-s3-bucket-name"` with your actual HTTP endpoint URL and S3 bucket ARN, respectively.

