To set up an AWS Route 53 hosted zone named `example53.com`, we will create a Terraform configuration that includes the necessary provider setup, a variable for the domain name, and the resource definition for the Route 53 zone.

Below is the complete Terraform HCL configuration:

```hcl
# Provider configuration for AWS
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-east-1"  # You can change this to your preferred region
}

# Variable for the domain name
variable "domain_name" {
  description = "The domain name for the Route 53 hosted zone"
  type        = string
  default     = "example53.com"
}

# Resource definition for the Route 53 hosted zone
resource "aws_route53_zone" "example_zone" {
  name = var.domain_name

  tags = {
    Name = "example53.com"
  }
}
```

