- **Provider Configuration**: The `provider` block specifies the AWS provider and sets the region to `us-east-1`. You can change this to any other region as per your requirement.
- **Variable Definition**: A variable `domain_name` is defined with a default value of `example53.com`. This allows flexibility if you want to use a different domain name in the future.
- **Route 53 Hosted Zone Resource**: The `aws_route53_zone` resource creates a new hosted zone in Route 53 with the name specified in the `domain_name` variable. Tags are added for better identification and management.

This configuration is ready to be deployed using Terraform. Ensure you have the necessary AWS credentials configured in your environment to allow Terraform to interact with your AWS account.

