The Terraform program I will define will create an AWS S3 bucket named `my_bucket` and attach a bucket policy that denies access from a specific IP address. The bucket policy will include a version number, an identifier, and a statement that specifies the denial of all S3 actions for the specified IP address. The `jsonencode` function will be used to encode the policy in JSON format.

Below is the complete Terraform HCL configuration:

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"  # You can change this to your preferred region
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket" "my_bucket" {
  bucket = "my_bucket"
}

variable "denied_ip" {
  description = "The IP address to deny access from"
  type        = string
  default     = "192.168.1.1"  # Replace with the IP address you want to deny
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket_policy" "deny_access_from_ip" {
  bucket = aws_s3_bucket.my_bucket.id

  policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17",
    Id      = "DenyAccessFromSpecificIP",
    Statement = [
      {
        Sid       = "DenySpecificIP",
        Effect    = "Deny",
        Principal = "*",
        Action    = "s3:*",
        Resource  = [
          aws_s3_bucket.my_bucket.arn,
          "${aws_s3_bucket.my_bucket.arn}/*"
        ],
        Condition = {
          IpAddress = {
            "aws:SourceIp" = var.denied_ip
          }
        }
      }
    ]
  })
}
```

This configuration sets up the AWS provider with a specified region, creates an S3 bucket named `my_bucket`, and attaches a policy that denies all S3 actions from a specified IP address. The IP address to be denied is provided via a variable with a default value, which you can customize as needed.

