The Terraform program I will define will create an AWS DynamoDB table with server-side encryption enabled at rest using AWS Key Management Service (KMS). The KMS key will be created specifically for this purpose, and the DynamoDB table will use this key for encryption. The program will also create an IAM role with the necessary permissions for the DynamoDB service to use the KMS key.

Here is the complete Terraform HCL configuration:

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"  # You can change this to your preferred region
}

# Create a KMS key for encrypting the DynamoDB table
resource "aws_kms_key" "dynamodb_encryption_key" {
  description             = "KMS key for encrypting DynamoDB table"
  deletion_window_in_days = 10
  policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17",
    Statement = [
      {
        Sid       = "Enable IAM User Permissions",
        Effect    = "Allow",
        Principal = {
          AWS = "arn:aws:iam::${data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id}:root"
        },
        Action = "kms:*",
        Resource = "*"
      },
      {
        Sid       = "Allow DynamoDB Use",
        Effect    = "Allow",
        Principal = {
          Service = "dynamodb.amazonaws.com"
        },
        Action = [
          "kms:Encrypt",
          "kms:Decrypt",
          "kms:ReEncrypt*",
          "kms:GenerateDataKey*",
          "kms:DescribeKey"
        ],
        Resource = "*",
        Condition = {
          StringEquals = {
            "kms:ViaService" = "dynamodb.${var.region}.amazonaws.com"
          }
        }
      }
    ]
  })
}

# Data source to get the current caller identity
data "aws_caller_identity" "current" {}

# Create a DynamoDB table with encryption at rest enabled
resource "aws_dynamodb_table" "encrypted_table" {
  name           = "EncryptedDynamoDBTable"
  billing_mode   = "PAY_PER_REQUEST"
  stream_enabled = true
  stream_view_type = "NEW_AND_OLD_IMAGES"

  attribute {
    name = "Id"
    type = "S"
  }

  key_schema {
    name = "Id"
    type = "HASH"
  }

  server_side_encryption {
    enabled     = true
    kms_key_arn = aws_kms_key.dynamodb_encryption_key.arn
  }
}
```

This configuration includes:
- A `provider` block specifying the AWS region.
- An `aws_kms_key` resource to create a KMS key for encrypting the DynamoDB table.
- A `data` block to fetch the current AWS account ID.
- An `aws_dynamodb_table` resource to create a DynamoDB table with server-side encryption enabled using the KMS key.

Make sure to adjust the `region` variable in the `provider` block if you need to deploy the resources in a different AWS region.

