  vpc_config {
    vpc_id     = aws_vpc.autograding_vpc.id
    subnets    = [aws_subnet.autograding_subnet.id]
    security_group_ids = [aws_security_group.autograding_sg.id]
  }

  tags = {
    Name        = "AutogradingProject"
    Environment = "production"
  }
}

# Variable for GitHub OAuth token (should be set securely)
variable "github_oauth_token" {
  description = "GitHub OAuth token for accessing the repository"
  type        = string
  sensitive   = true
}
```

### Explanation:
- **S3 Bucket**: Used to store the results of the autograding process.
- **IAM Role**: Allows the CodeBuild project to access the S3 bucket and perform necessary actions.
- **VPC and Subnet**: Creates a VPC and a subnet within it to run the CodeBuild project in an isolated environment.
- **Security Group**: Controls inbound and outbound traffic to the CodeBuild project, ensuring it does not have access to the internet.
- **CodeBuild Project**: Configured to pull code from a GitHub repository and run it in the isolated VPC environment, storing the results in the S3 bucket.

Make sure to replace `https://github.com/your-repo/autograder.git` with the actual URL of your GitHub repository and provide a secure method to pass the `github_oauth_token` variable.

