The Terraform program I will define will create an egress-only internet gateway named "pike" and associate it with a specified VPC. This setup allows IPv6-enabled instances within the VPC to send traffic to the internet while preventing any inbound traffic from the internet. The egress-only internet gateway will be tagged with "permissions".

Below is the Terraform HCL configuration:

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"  # You can change this to your preferred region
}

variable "vpc_id" {
  description = "The ID of the VPC to which the egress-only internet gateway will be attached"
  type        = string
  default     = "vpc-0123456789abcdef0"  # Replace with your VPC ID
}

resource "aws_egress_only_internet_gateway" "pike" {
  vpc_id = var.vpc_id

  tags = {
    Name        = "pike"
    permissions = "egress-only"
  }
}
```

### Explanation:
- **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured with a default region (`us-west-2`). You can change this to any region that suits your needs.
- **Variable `vpc_id`**: This variable holds the ID of the VPC to which the egress-only internet gateway will be attached. A default value is provided, but you should replace it with the actual VPC ID you intend to use.
- **Resource `aws_egress_only_internet_gateway`**: This resource creates the egress-only internet gateway named "pike" and associates it with the specified VPC. It also applies tags to the gateway for better identification and management.

This configuration is ready to be deployed using Terraform version `~> 1.9.8` and the AWS provider version `~> 5.75`. Make sure to replace the default `vpc_id` with the actual VPC ID where you want to deploy the egress-only internet gateway.

